0,$ which of the following is an inhibited decay equation?" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321791 1113 #uuid "6f61f141-3dc0-53a6-8909-845a088a0525" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321791 1145 "An inhibited decay equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=-k(y-a),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $y>a$ for all $t>0.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only inhibited decay equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=840-28y.\n$$\n\nTo see this, let's factor the right-hand side of the equation. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=-28(y-30).\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=28,$ and $a=30.$ Note that for inhibited decay, we must have $y>30$ for all $t>0.$" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321793 13194139534948 true] [17592186321792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321794 13194139534948 true] [17592186321792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321795 13194139534948 true] [17592186321792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321796 13194139534948 true] [17592186321792 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321797 13194139534948 true] [17592186321792 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534948 true] [17592186321792 1041 "selection" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321792 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321795 13194139534948 true] [17592186321792 1110 #uuid "887bbde7-4844-5579-8445-8e33a034a40e" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321793 1034 "\\frac{dy}{dt}=28{y}^{2}-840" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321793 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321793 1111 #uuid "75c50c6a-85f9-5fc6-a66c-431f9860354e" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321794 1034 "\\frac{dy}{dt}=840y-28{y}^{2}" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321794 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321794 1111 #uuid "3809d0a6-7a4f-59f3-90c1-7eb586d58bfe" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321795 1034 "\\frac{dy}{dt}=840-28y" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321795 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321795 1111 #uuid "a2206494-11d5-5ec6-8fdd-efc01cc18ab3" 13194139534948 true] [175921863