es Celsius, and $t>0$ is the time in minutes. If the room temperature is ${19}^{∘}\\text{C},$ which differential equation could be used to model the water temperature? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality." 13194139534948 true] [17592186321819 1113 #uuid "ae2e994f-7344-5287-a621-1bc5f34b7d82" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321819 1145 "Newton's law of cooling states that the rate at which the temperature $T(t)$ of a body changes is proportional to the difference between its temperature and its surroundings. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-{T}_{S}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${T}_{S}$ is the temperature of the surroundings, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, ${T}_{S}={19}^{∘}\\text{C},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-19).\n$$" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321820 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321821 13194139534948 true] [17592186321820 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321822 13194139534948 true] [17592186321820 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321823 13194139534948 true] [17592186321820 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321824 13194139534948 true] [17592186321820 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321825 13194139534948 true] [17592186321820 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534948 true] [17592186321820 1041 "selection" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321820 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321825 13194139534948 true] [17592186321820 1110 #uuid "5d3c5875-313e-56dc-bd36-dd119157f06e" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321821 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-90(T-19)" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321821 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321821 1111 #uuid "6191616a-cb79-54d3-83b4-11b1fcf49e21" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321822 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-90k(T-19)" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321822 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321822 1111 #uuid "1f510184-ea1e-5a55-9996-200671c6d31f" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321823 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-90)" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321823 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321823 1111 #uuid "c0c1a33e-4340-5e63-aa54-83440875ed46" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321824 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-19k(T-90)" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321824 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321824 1111 #uuid "13652fb1-f84d-590d-8220-90a32d70b95b" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321825 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-19)" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321825 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321825 1111 #uuid "cc7520b1-5d34-588d-b6c7-d81d8a574822" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321826 1017 #edb/ref 17592186321827 13194139534948 true] [17592186321826 1089 "q-107118" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321826 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534948 true] [17592186321826 1100 "The temperature $T(t),$ in degrees Celsius, of a cooling iron can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dT}{dt}=-0.1(T-28)\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, measured in minutes. If the initial temperature of the iron is ${140}^{∘}C,$ calculate its temperature after $5$ minutes. Round your answer to the nearest integer." 13194139534948 true] [17592186321826 1113 #uuid "6b4e1aaa-5dbc-5088-a3aa-1be98695474d" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321826 1145 "We're told that the temperature of the cooling iron is modeled by the inhibited decay equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dT}{dt}=-0.1(T-28).\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate our differential equation by separating the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dT}{T-28} & =-0.1\\,dt \\\\ \\int \\frac{dT}{T-28} & =-\\int 0.1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|T-28| & =-0.1t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is the solution to an inhibited decay equation, we have $T-28>0$ for all $t>0.$\nNext, we solve for $T(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T-28 & ={e}^{-0.1t+C} \\\\ T-28 & ={e}^{C}{e}^{-0.1t} \\\\ T-28 & =K{e}^{-0.1t} \\\\ T & =28+K{e}^{-0.1t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{C}$ is a constant of integration. \n\nWe're told that the initial temperature of the iron was ${140}^{∘}C.$ So, we apply the initial condition $T(0)=140,$ and solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}140 & =28+K{e}^{0} \\\\ 140 & =28+K \\\\ K & =112\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is\n\n$$\nT(t)=28+112{e}^{-0.1t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the temperature of the iron after $t=5$ minutes is\n\n$$\nT(5)=28+112{e}^{-0.1\\cdot 5}≈{96}^{∘}\\text{C},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139534948 true] [17592186321827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321828 13194139534948 true] [17592186321827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321829 13194139534948 true] [17592186321827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321830 13194139534948 true] [17592186321827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321831 13194139534948 true] [17592186321827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321832 13194139534948 true] [17592186321827 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534948 true] [17592186321827 1041 "selection" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321827 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321828 13194139534948 true] [17592186321827 1110 #uuid "fc2435ba-70d9-51e5-b442-284e42d013fd" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321828 1034 "{96}^{∘}\\text{C}" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321828 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321828 1111 #uuid "327b36d3-819c-5438-8676-c37d16c08a13" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321829 1034 "{76}^{∘}\\text{C}" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321829 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321829 1111 #uuid "d26ecd7d-434d-58ba-932e-05a9fcbcd237" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321830 1034 "{79}^{∘}\\text{C}" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321830 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321830 1111 #uuid "e40cf18d-65d9-52e2-8fbc-73e0e1d53b21" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321831 1034 "{81}^{∘}\\text{C}" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321831 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321831 1111 #uuid "5edb4d4e-1d84-5cd0-bd44-852653396e18" 1319413953