of the cake after $t=8$ minutes is\n\n$$\nT(8)=70+270{e}^{-0.09\\cdot 8}≈{201}^{∘}\\text{F},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139534948 true] [17592186321834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321835 13194139534948 true] [17592186321834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321836 13194139534948 true] [17592186321834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321837 13194139534948 true] [17592186321834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321838 13194139534948 true] [17592186321834 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321839 13194139534948 true] [17592186321834 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534948 true] [17592186321834 1041 "selection" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321834 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321837 13194139534948 true] [17592186321834 1110 #uuid "a791edc1-78b5-56ba-b67e-872ee0d0c530" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321835 1034 "{189}^{∘}\\text{F}" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321835 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321835 1111 #uuid "52cdde1c-82d5-5b64-b35a-706e91dbd8e9" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321836 1034 "{198}^{∘}\\text{F}" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321836 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321836 1111 #uuid "7371e460-d8f2-57cb-a9d9-2aca752430dd" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321837 1034 "{201}^{∘}\\text{F}" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321837 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321837 1111 #uuid "673f9fdd-d45e-5e35-9a8f-8fadfbef6844" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321838 1034 "{223}^{∘}\\text{F}" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321838 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321838 1111 #uuid "6e67afe9-ad00-5c70-ab76-7a59e39a896b" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321839 1034 "{194}^{∘}\\text{F}" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321839 1111 #uuid "81fb3f4d-5f1f-535b-a29d-b61b1391cb75" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321840 1017 #edb/ref 17592186321841 13194139534948 true] [17592186321840 1089 "q-107125" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321840 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534948 true] [17592186321840 1100 "Simon measures the temperature of the tea in his cup, and the thermometer displays a reading of ${60}^{∘}C.$ After $10$ minutes, Simon repeats the measurement and the thermometer displays a reading of  ${52}^{∘}C.$ To the nearest minute, how long does it take for the tea to decrease its temperature to ${40}^{∘}C$ if the temperature in the room is ${28}^{∘}C?$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that the temperature $T(t)$ of the tea in Simon's cup decreases at a rate that obeys Newton's law of cooling, where $T$ is measured in degrees Celsius and $t>0$ is the time, in minutes, since the first measurement.*" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321840 1113 #uuid "fee906ee-def7-5194-a87e-a1f77108aa56" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321840 1145 "Newton's law of cooling states that the rate at which the temperature $T(t)$ of a body changes is proportional to the difference between its temperature and its surroundings. Therefore, we have the inhibited decay equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-{T}_{S}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${T}_{S}$ is the temperature of the surroundings, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, ${T}_{S}={28}^{∘}\\text{C},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-28).\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate our differential equation by separating the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dT}{T-28} & =-k\\,dt \\\\ \\int \\frac{dT}{T-28} & =-k\\int dt \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|T-28| & =-kt+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is the solution to an inhibited decay equation, we have $T-28>0$ for all $t>0.$\nNext, we solve for $T(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T-28 & ={e}^{-kt+C} \\\\ T-28 & ={e}^{C}{e}^{-kt} \\\\ T-28 & =K{e}^{-kt} \\\\ T & =28+K{e}^{-kt}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{C}$ is a constant of integration. \n\nWe're told that the initial temperature reading was ${60}^{∘}C.$ So, we apply the initial condition $T(0)=60,$ and solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}60 & =28+K{e}^{0} \\\\ 60 & =28+K \\\\ K & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following expression for $T(t):$\n\n$$\nT(t)=28+32{e}^{-kt}\n$$\n\nWe're also told that, after $10$ minutes, the thermometer reading is ${52}^{∘}C.$ So, applying the condition $T(10)=52,$ we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}52 & =28+32{e}^{-10k} \\\\ 24 & =32{e}^{-10k} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & ={e}^{-10k} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}) & =-10k \\\\ k & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the temperature of the tea is ${40}^{∘}C.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({t}_{1}) & =40 \\\\ 28+32{e}^{-k{t}_{1}} & =40 \\\\ 32{e}^{-k{t}_{1}} & =12 \\\\ {e}^{-k{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{3}{8} \\\\ -k{t}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{8}) \\\\ {t}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting in our value for $k,$ we conclude that the tea will have a temperature of ${40}^{∘}C$ after\n\n$$\n{t}_{1}=\\frac{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{8})}{-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})}≈34\\,\\text{min},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest minute." 13194139534948 true] [17592186321841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321842 13194139534948 true] [17592186321841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321843 13194139534948 true] [17592186321841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321844 13194139534948 true] [17592186321841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321845 13194139534948 true] [17592186321841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321846 13194139534948 true] [17592186321841 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534948 true] [17592186321841 1041 "selection" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321841 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321845 13194139534948 true] [17592186321841 1110 #uuid "7443f0d6-6378-52ac-8682-db6bd720f948" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321842 1034 "23\\,\\text{min}" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321842 1111 #uuid "409ba1ce-74ab-529c-bfb5-77536e76250e" 13194139534948 true] [1759218