bited decay equation, we have $T-21>0$ for all $t>0.$\nNext, we solve for $T(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T-21 & ={e}^{-0.12t+C} \\\\ T-21 & ={e}^{C}{e}^{-0.12t} \\\\ T-21 & =K{e}^{-0.12t} \\\\ T & =21+K{e}^{-0.12t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{C}$ is a constant of integration. \n\nWe're told that the initial temperature of the compressor was ${65}^{∘}C.$ So, we apply the initial condition $T(0)=65,$ and solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}65 & =21+K{e}^{0} \\\\ 65 & =21+K \\\\ K & =44\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is\n\n$$\nT(t)=21+44{e}^{-0.12t}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the temperature of the compressor after $t=8$ minutes is\n\n$$\nT(8)=21+44{e}^{-0.12\\cdot 8}≈{38}^{∘}\\text{C},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139534948 true] [17592186321848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321849 13194139534948 true] [17592186321848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321850 13194139534948 true] [17592186321848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321851 13194139534948 true] [17592186321848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321852 13194139534948 true] [17592186321848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321853 13194139534948 true] [17592186321848 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534948 true] [17592186321848 1041 "selection" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321848 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321852 13194139534948 true] [17592186321848 1110 #uuid "2b546eac-0f98-51fa-8f14-4ed027e28fc9" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321849 1034 "{31}^{∘}\\text{C}" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321849 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321849 1111 #uuid "1aa5f8e7-ec62-5131-9299-59a9b45fea82" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321850 1034 "{43}^{∘}\\text{C}" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321850 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321850 1111 #uuid "a9bb5d32-72cd-58e5-879d-f1cc274c62fb" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321851 1034 "{58}^{∘}\\text{C}" 13194139534948 true] [17592186321851 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534948 true] [17592186321851 1111 #uuid 